# Shell scripts must keep LF in the working tree, not just in the repo.
#
# cloud/entrypoint.sh is the ENTRYPOINT of the cloud server image. Built from a
# checkout where core.autocrlf turned it into CRLF, the shebang ends up as
# `#!/bin/bash\r` and the container dies with
# `exec /entrypoint.sh: no such file or directory` — which says nothing about
# line endings and costs an hour to recognise.
*.sh text eol=lf
